## Full Eternity Bands as Wedding Rings

Some buyers want the continuous diamond wall of a full eternity band rather than the 7-stone format. The full eternity makes a stronger visual statement and uses 12–16 small stones instead of 7 larger ones.

The key caveat is The No-Resize Rule. A full eternity band cannot be resized after purchase because stones circle the entire band with no metal gap. Confirm your ring size three times on three separate days before ordering.

A 0.5 size error on an eternity band means a new ring, not an alteration. There is no resizing option because any cut would remove a stone. A 7-stone band gives you 1–2 full sizes of adjustment room — an eternity band gives you none.

If you are between sizes, size up for an eternity band. A slightly loose band that spins slightly is wearable. A band that cannot slide over the knuckle is not — and it cannot be made larger after the fact.

